we begin with an urgent plea on gun  control from president biden in a rare  prime time address from the white house  using candles as a backdrop the  president urged congress to act to  finally reform gun laws after a series  of mass shootings in buffalo uvalde  tulsa and dozens of other communities  the imagery of crisis violence and grief  has become all too familiar in american  life nancy cordes joins us from the  white house nancy good morning  good morning nate this may have been the  most emphatic speech this president has  delivered when it comes to guns it's an  issue he's been reluctant to dwell on  until now because the chances of passing  anything are just so slim but that was  before 19 third and fourth graders were  gunned down in texas using the kind of  weapon that used to be banned  let us finally do something after a  month of mass shootings in uvalde  buffalo tulsa and more president biden  pleaded with republicans to support new  gun control laws too many other everyday  places that have become killing fields  battlefields here in america his  ambitious wish list includes a ban on  high-capacity magazines universal  background checks new safe storage laws  and red flag laws and a return to the  assault weapons ban that he helped to  pass in 1994. if we can't ban assault  weapons then we should raise the aids to  purchase them from 18 to 21. he pointed  to studies that show mass shooting  deaths tripled after congress left the  assault weapons ban lapse in 2004 the  second amendment like all other rights  is not absolute this isn't about taking  to anyone's rights  it's about protecting children but in  the house the battle lines haven't  changed this is on our watch  where is the outrage how dare you  you think we don't have hearts house  democrats and republicans debated a  major package of gun laws thursday for  nearly 10 hours we are paying  for this deadly culture with the lives  of the american people this bill would  not stop the terrible events it wouldn't  harden schools but it will sure take  away the rights  of the american people who follow the  law in the senate a bipartisan group  says it's making progress on measures to  address red flag laws school safety and  mental illness every day that goes by we  get closer to an agreement not further  away  but that agreement if it comes together  will not include some of these major gun  safety measures that the president is  calling for like raising the purchasing  age for assault weapons from 18 to 21.  some states however are moving ahead on  their own just yesterday new york  state's legislature passed a bill that  would do just that and it now heads to  the governor's desk tony  as with so much else else in this  country it heads to the states and then  maybe the courts nancy thank you very  much we appreciate it
 

